{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness","id":95460,"title":"A More Logical World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-21T01:27:37-07:00","id":95460,"title":"A More Logical World of Darkness","content":"<i>Some White Wolf authors wrote as if each gameline existed in its own universe, yet other White Wolf authors wrote as if all of the supernatural populations coexisted on a single crowded planet. This lack of consistent centralized supervision resulted in a World of Darkness that was neither entirely separate parallel worlds nor an entirely unified world. The easiest solution is to separate the gamelines, but for those who played on a single crowded planet...</i><br /> <br /> The classic World of Darkness could not logically exist as it was described. To see this most clearly we simply look at the highest global powers. According to the classic <i>Vampire</i> game, elder vampires rule the world (as wielding entire nations as a personal resource is an Elder Background), but according to the classic <i>Mage</i> game, the Technocracy rules the world (as they supposedly control consensual reality itself). These two facts cannot coexist on a single planet, so what this really means is that THE fundamental power struggle in the classic World of Darkness would actually be vampires versus Technocrats; all of the supernatural beings in the World of Darkness would be affected by and drawn into this one core conflict of the global supernatural super powers.<br /> <br /> The name of the elder vampires' umbrella corporation would be... Pentex. With elder vampires already ruling the world, Pentex would have never come into existence outside of the actions of elder vampires. (If a Sabbat sect ever formed at all as an intermediary step, during the Industrial Age it would have modernized into corporate Pentex by necessity.) The vampiric bloodline primarily responsible for forming Pentex are... the Baali. No other bloodline would have more connection to the Wyrm or more mastery of Fomori production than the Baali. The Antediluvian of the Baali is... Azaneal (a.k.a. Lucien, Lasombra, Shaitan, and Baal). (The Deceiver deceived us!) The Lasombra and Baali both wield the powers of the Abyss, because both bloodlines descend from the same Antediluvian. Peter Culliford, the Executive Director of Pentex, was a mortal Inquisition torturer and executioner who became possessed by an Abyssal \u201cdemon\u201d named... Azaneal. In the <i>Mage</i> game some spirits have Mage Spheres, so elder dark thaumaturges could gain Mage Spheres by transforming themselves into Fomori (which would effectively make them Nephandi).<br /> <br /> The primary military arm of the Technocracy consists of the technomantic cyborgs of Iteration-X. With the body of their Technocratic god-machine (Autochthon/Weaver) as their home-base, the martial power which is Iteration-X would be the most powerful Convention in the Technocracy. (Defining Iteration-X as the most powerful Technocratic Convention does not alter the power of the Technocracy, so this portion regarding Iteration-X can be ignored in the larger argument.) Also, it is not likely that the Mechanicians would have ever changed their name to something awkward like \u201cIteration-X\u201d.<br /> <br /> Vampires comprise the army of the Wyrm, and the Technocracy is the army of the Weaver. The Wyld, being the remaining god of the warring Triat, would also have its own army. The Changing Breeds are the descendants of Lunar Exalteds who long ago were exiled into the Wyld Lands and gained shapechanging powers from the Wyld. (The Changing Breed who maintain the closest affinity to the Wyld are the Nuwisha; modern coyote and wolf populations have interbred such that Nuwisha are effectively Ragabash werewolves.) Changelings are Wyld spirits who reincarnate into mortal bodies. Changeling souls, drawn by Wyld energy, would preferentially reincarnate into Changing Breed bodies (especially Nuwisha and Ragabash) when available, which effectively blends Changelings and Changing Breeds into a single population (\u201cChangeling Breeds\u201d). The Changelings are really the only other supernatural population who have a large-scale organizational structure, so the social structure of the hybrid \u201cChangeling Breeds\u201d would mostly likely be something akin to the Court, Kingdom, and House structures of the Changelings. The dominant Court would be the Unseelie Court or the Shadow Court, by necessity. In the <i>Mage</i> game some spirits have Mage Spheres, so elder theurges could gain Mage Spheres by transforming themselves into Gorgons, which would effectively make them Marauder mages. Without nearly godlike Marauder archmages among them to match Technocratic archmages and vampire elders, the hybrid \u201cChangeling Breeds\u201d would be trampled in the conflict between the Technocracy and the elder vampires.<br /> <br /> The supernatural group occupying the middle ground are the Tradition mages. With Gaia as a source of power, the Earth-mages [a.k.a Verbena, Dreamspeakers, etc.] would be the most powerful and populous of the Tradition mages. In the <i>Mage</i> game some spirits have Mage Spheres, so Gaia could create Earth-mages by transforming a human into a Kami.<br /> <br /> The Material Universe which contains Earth is touched by three Zones, each of which leads to its corresponding Shenti (\u201ccelestial body\u201d): the Dreaming which leads to Arcadia (a moon which orbits Radiance/Wyld), the [Digital] Web which leads to Autocthonia (the machine-body of the Weaver), and the Shadowlands which lead to Malfeas (the planetoid which inexplicably hovers over the Abyss/Wyrm).<br /> <br /> I'm sure that I'm not the only Storyteller to have made corrections to the illogic that permeated the classic World of Darkness. I decided to take my corrections to their ultimate conclusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2509,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","user":"Thanateros","date":".  Expanded Azaneal's aliases 05-09-2014, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T01:44:57-07:00","id":95463,"title":"","content":"1) Ravnos versus Technocracy. Technocracy won(barely, but they won). Just saying.<br /> <br /> 2) What, we can't have eight or nine mindbreakingly large powers waging a shadow war with each other over entire spectrums of reality for control over everything? Since when?<br /> <br /> 3) You want to argue logic in a world defined by a conflict between conscious and unconscious subjective world-shaping understanding? A world that began as multi- layered, co-existent mess where in everything kind of was at the exact same time? You want to make a <i>gothic-punk cosmic horror setting from the 90s</i> logical?<br /> <br /> Sir, I've read your thing, and I don't know oWoD well enough to critique it wholly, but it does seem to me like you are beginning from a bad conceit built from faulty reasoning, both from an in-universe standpoint and from a narrative conceit standpoint, and tumble down the hill from there.<br /> <br /> I can, of course, be entirely wrong, and I invite others who know the setting better to explore the idea-but man do I think the odds are against you.<br /> <br /> PS: Being facetious, besides, we all know everything is mages. It's fucking mages.<br /> <br /> I kid of course, but, well.<br /> <br /> Another PS: I mean, hell, this world has, like, eight distinct ends? And they all happen at once? And that's played with a straight face? Logic kind of gets face raped with that alone.<br /> <br /> (Gehenna, Apocalypse, Ascension or whatever it is, Doomsday, Long Winter, Twilight of the Gods, Armageddon, Going Westward-am I missing any?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-21-2014, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T03:59:36-07:00","id":95501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=95463#post95463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...it does seem to me like you are beginning from a bad conceit built from faulty reasoning</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this &quot;bad conceit&quot;, and why is it bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T04:14:57-07:00","id":95504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=95463#post95463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Ravnos versus Technocracy. Technocracy won(barely, but they won). Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Staying on the side lines while Kuei-Jin do the heavy lifting and then bomb everything, isn't winning a fight, it's not fighting at all...<br /> <br /> <br /> But, I agree in general.<br /> <br /> Also the first post doesn't incorporate exceptions to general statements.<br /> <br /> Do the Vampire Elders rule over nations and have the ability to wreck whole economies ? Sure.<br /> Are they beyond making bad decisions, having bad luck, having problems to find proper retainers? They aren't.<br /> <br /> Neither is the Technocracy really...<br /> <br /> As far as Pentex goes, there is a vampire there, sure, but those fellows are for the most part humans backed by evil gods, possibly from beyond creation. While one could call Vampire elders &quot;gods&quot;, for all their power compared to a human, these beings can imbue humans with matching powers - while themselves unable to affect the world directly.<br /> <br /> For a vampire elder, a decade isn't that long. So imagine his surprise, if he compares 2004's google ($23 Billion market capitalisation) to today's google ($397 Billion market capitalisation). So, could a company, even a big player, rise over night, without the vampire elders making sure they control it completely? Sure, it could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T05:15:17-07:00","id":95532,"title":"","content":"Vampire elders <i>control</i> very little. What they do is <i>influence</i>, which is quite different. No vampire on the planet can just call up the White House, say &quot;Hey, invade Panama for me will ya?&quot; and have it happen. It doesn't work like that. It's like a guy pushing a car. Sure, he has some impact on what direction the car goes, but the weight of the car and the shape of the road are bigger forces. It's still ridiculously impressive compared to most of us - we would be ants trying to the car - but true control is impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T05:42:12-07:00","id":95541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness#post95460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The classic World of Darkness could not logically exist as it was described. To see this most clearly we simply look at the highest global powers. According to the classic <i>Vampire</i> game, elder vampires rule the world (as wielding entire nations as a personal resource is an Elder Background), but according to the classic <i>Mage</i> game, the Technocracy rules the world (as they supposedly control consensual reality itself). These two facts cannot coexist on a single planet, so what this really means is that THE fundamental power struggle in the classic World of Darkness would actually be vampires versus Technocrats; all of the supernatural beings in the World of Darkness would be affected by and drawn into this one core conflict of the global supernatural super powers.<br /> *snip*<br /> I'm sure that I'm not the only Storyteller to have made corrections to the illogic that permeated the classic World of Darkness. I decided to take my corrections to their ultimate conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, your opening paragraph:<br /> \u200bElder Vampires control governments, and many corporations. Technocracy controls the peoples belief in how the world works, manipulates the governments, and owns many corporations. There would be times that the Vampire corporations and Technocratic corporations, kind of Shadowrun-style at times even. There would be times that the Technocracy and the Vampires would get into conflicts due to each trying to manipulate the same person for different ends. But on the whole, the two groups have different, but not always necessarily opposing, goals.<br /> \u200bIt makes me think of how clan-book Assamite discusses their relationship with Ravnos: &quot;We stay out of their way, and they stay out of ours. Occasionally, we'll have to kill one of their younger, stupider kleptomaniacs. Occasionally, they'll have to kill one of our younger, stupider sociopaths. It's an equitable arrangement.&quot;<br /> Neither group has the power to move against the other. Neither group has the inclination to do so, either. But they do, to a certain extent, check each other.<br /> <br /> Second, your attempt at re-structuring the world:<br /> Whatever. I don't always agree with the cWoD meta, but you are trying to change it drastically, use the Triat, as you fundamentally shift the entire method that the Garou interact with them, keep the Baali as you fundamentally shift the entire structure of Vampires, their clans, and their history, and so-forth.<br /> <br /> \u200bI am all for complete restructuring of a setting to suit my needs as a DM/GM/ST, but I also know the difference between saying &quot;We're playing in the Forgotten Realms&quot;, and saying &quot;We're playing in a custom world based on the Forgotten Realms CS&quot;. And that is what you are doing. You are not trying to fix the illogical points of the cWoD, you are taking elements of the cWoD and using them to make something completely your own that has only the most superficial resemblance to what you are deconstructing. Additionally, in doing a complete deconstruct / reconstruct, instead of fixing the portions of the cannon that are inconsistent / inconceivable, you have made a whole new cannon that is just as prone to / full of errors.<br /> <br /> Finally, your ending statements:<br /> \u200bYes, I am sure that other STs have. I, for one, have done both methods. I have run games that correct the portions of the cannon that are counter-intuitive, whether that be: to remove something from the present due to back-story; remove / change the past to suit the present; as the above options, but by adding instead of subtracting; or by many combinations of the above. I have also done as you have, and used the available mechanics from the various systems to make a new setting, either whole-cloth, or just as you did by deconstructing / reconstructing.<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> On the whole though, I do not like your word choice to say that you &quot;corrected&quot; it, when it does seem as if you simply completely restructured everything.<br /> Sometimes a house is so badly damaged that you cannot fix it, and you must tear down and re-build. But if you tore down a house and re-built it, that is not the same as fixing what was wrong, that is eliminating them through a different means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T05:58:34-07:00","id":95546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness#post95460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The classic World of Darkness could not logically exist as it was described. To see this most clearly we simply look at the highest global powers. According to the classic <i>Vampire</i> game, elder vampires rule the world (as wielding entire nations as a personal resource is an Elder Background), but according to the classic <i>Mage</i> game, the Technocracy rules the world (as they supposedly control consensual reality itself). These two facts cannot coexist on a single planet, so what this really means is that THE fundamental power struggle in the classic World of Darkness would actually be vampires versus Technocrats; all of the supernatural beings in the World of Darkness would be affected by and drawn into this one core conflict of the global supernatural super powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're making an even more fundamental assumption: you're assuming all the gamelines described take place in the same world. I haven't read the fiction, but based on what I know of the core books of various lines, that's really not a valid assumption. Actually, isn't the assumption that it <i>isn't</i> all the same world? I vaguely remember something about Lupines (werewolves in Masquerade) explicitly being different to Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T06:11:47-07:00","id":95553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=95546#post95546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're making an even more fundamental assumption: you're assuming all the gamelines described take place in the same world. I haven't read the fiction, but based on what I know of the core books of various lines, that's really not a valid assumption. Actually, isn't the assumption that it <i>isn't</i> all the same world? I vaguely remember something about Lupines (werewolves in Masquerade) explicitly being different to Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best explanation of this I ever heard is that cWoD exists in a multiverse and each game line is a bubble in a grouping of bubbles. What exists in one bubble has reflections in others, but they are not necessarily the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T07:22:32-07:00","id":95597,"title":"","content":"It does not need an explanation. The game lines are separate. If you choose to treat them otherwise, the onus is on you to make it &quot;logical&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:28:20-07:00","id":95663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=95504#post95504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Pentex goes, there is a vampire there, sure, but those fellows are for the most part humans backed by evil gods, possibly from beyond creation. While one could call Vampire elders &quot;gods&quot;, for all their power compared to a human, these beings can imbue humans with matching powers - while themselves unable to affect the world directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're explicitly powerful spirits of corruption. The ruined parts of the destroyer that self-servingly perpetuate its original error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T15:52:34-07:00","id":96011,"title":"","content":"For any crossover game, you have to decide first which one's secrets are actually true, and which one's secrets <i>may</i> be true only if they support the thesis of the primary game. None of them are much more than superficially compatible, as written, and frankly most of the official crossover rules were hasty last-minute additions, the least mechanically sound parts of a set of games notorious for poor system quality. A Mage Game featuring Vampires is a totally different beast than a Vampire Game featuring Mages. And a game featuring both Mages and Vampires as equally important things is going to be neck deep in homebrew. A WoD game featuring all factions and splats, and trying to share narrative primacy between them, will require a near complete rewrite of the setting.<br /> <br /> And in any case, descriptions of the degree of control exerted by any of the Hidden Master of the WoD were pretty slipshod and hyperbolic. Keep in mind that the WoD was also notoriously bad about giving any tonal distinctions between data meant for setting the mood for players, and data meant to provide tools to storytellers. When you read that (splat X) has secret control of (nation/industry/religion/faction), that's almost always being presented as an attempt to establish an atmosphere of paranoia for PCs. Closer looks at actual Hidden Master NPCs always display much looser, more subtle power structures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":615,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","user":"The Hanged Man","date":". 03-22-2014, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T16:13:45-07:00","id":96027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Earth-mages [a.k.a Verbena] </div> </div> </div>Would that not be the Dreamspeakers? Their background actually makes direct reference to Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T17:05:28-07:00","id":96057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96027#post96027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that not be the Dreamspeakers? Their background actually makes direct reference to Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even then, they reshape reality, so they aren't really very Gaian at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T22:42:04-07:00","id":96198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96011#post96011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you read that (splat X) has secret control of (nation/industry/religion/faction), that's almost always being presented as an attempt to establish an atmosphere of paranoia for PCs. Closer looks at actual Hidden Master NPCs always display much looser, more subtle power structures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that any tribe/clan/tradition/kithbook is propaganda. As well as many other books. I do wish, honestly, that the WoD had Player / ST books that were separate. But of course that never stops players from knowing the stuff in the ST books, as happens in other games. Maybe why I dream of running games where the players know nothing about the universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I may be a control freak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T00:48:35-07:00","id":96229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=95553#post95553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best explanation of this I ever heard is that cWoD exists in a multiverse and each game line is a bubble in a grouping of bubbles. What exists in one bubble has reflections in others, but they are not necessarily the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to the lack of cohesiveness among the games, the multiverse that you describe is the other sensible option I proposed [in another thread] for resolving the numerous contradictions. White Wolf really did make the mistake though of cramming all of the games onto the same planet then later clumsily backpedal to erect and maintain separations that strain credibility. White Wolf never described multiple Worlds of Darkness; they only ever described a single World of Darkness, such as in the <i>World of Darkness</i> sourcebook itself. The multiverse option is certainly the easier of the two options for resolving contradictions, as it does not require the restructuring that I did above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T01:54:13-07:00","id":96246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZhyzhaksMate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=95541#post95541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are not trying to fix the illogical points of the cWoD, you are taking elements of the cWoD and using them to make something completely your own that has only the most superficial resemblance to what you are deconstructing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was expecting that the lengthiest objection would come from a <i>Werewolf</i> fan, since the Garou are the most impacted by my proposed corrections. My proposals are in no way a negative evaluation against your favorite game. Perhaps ironically, if a chronomantic paradox were to wipe out all of the White Wolf game lines except for one, classic <i>Werewolf</i> would probably get my vote for survival, due largely to the Triat being my favorite pantheon of any fictional universe. (My signature Thanateros character is an &quot;aborted&quot; proto-Maeljin of Desire.)<br /> <br /> I see the distinction that you are trying to make between merely fixing and completely restructuring, but what you are missing is that the classic World of Darkness as a whole was just so deeply flawed logically that a sufficiently thorough &quot;fixing&quot; ends up being a complete restructuring. Deep flaws require equally deep corrections. If your fixing of the classic World of Darkness does not result in a complete restructuring, then you left at least one major contradiction unresolved. <br /> <br /> Resolving contradictions requires that choices be made. I chose to focus on the scale of the global superpowers and use the Triat as a unifying background premise, which then informed all of my subsequent decisions. Other Storytellers could choose a different focus and make different choices than what I did and still end up with fully cohesive worlds not resembling the one I described above. (Alternately, we could just employ a simple multiple parallel Earths cosmology like what Derzhuzad describes to resolve all contradictions between the games.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T02:34:07-07:00","id":96253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rderekp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96198#post96198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wish, honestly, that the WoD had Player / ST books that were separate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at my bookshelf of cWOD books... I'm pretty sure I see a few books clearly labeled as &quot;Storyteller&quot; and others as &quot;Players.&quot;<br /> <br /> Snark aside, I can't really blame them for having most books be ST/player divide neutral. Most cWOD are short enough as it was without cutting them in half to have player-relevant-only books and ST books as a separate thing. Most of the cWOD splat books are, what, ~100 pages? There's just not enough there for cutting it up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96229#post96229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf really did make the mistake though of cramming all of the games onto the same planet then later clumsily backpedal to erect and maintain separations that strain credibility. White Wolf never described multiple Worlds of Darkness; they only ever described a single World of Darkness, such as in the <i>World of Darkness</i> sourcebook itself. The multiverse option is certainly the easier of the two options for resolving contradictions, as it does not require the restructuring that I did above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, your timeline here is a bit off.<br /> <br /> Way back in 1e, White Wolf started quite adamant about the multiverse of the WOD. The original idea for the WOD was that each of the game lines would be exist in a separate variant on the same universe. It wasn't until late 1e/early 2e that there was a move to start presenting everything as being compatible; but the damage was already done. By the time things were solidly into 2e and beyond, everything was being written with an eye towards facilitating it all happening in one big crowded world, while each game-line persisted with the multiverse based core premise they began with. And that's were pretty much all of the contradictory mess comes in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T02:52:44-07:00","id":96256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96253#post96253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Way back in 1e, White Wolf started quite adamant about the multiverse of the WOD. The original idea for the WOD was that each of the game lines would be exist in a separate variant on the same universe. It wasn't until late 1e/early 2e that there was a move to start presenting everything as being compatible; but the damage was already done. By the time things were solidly into 2e and beyond, everything was being written with an eye towards facilitating it all happening in one big crowded world, while each game-line persisted with the multiverse based core premise they began with. And that's were pretty much all of the contradictory mess comes in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that correction and elaboration! My interaction with the World of Darkness began with 2e; I have not interacted with very many people who even remember 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T09:38:56-07:00","id":96382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96246#post96246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was expecting that the lengthiest objection would come from a <i>Werewolf</i> fan, since the Garou are the most impacted by my proposed corrections.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) I am not a fan of any one game line moreso than any other. I like them all. I prefer the mechanics of Vampire, and the freedom of Mage, and the sheer satiation of tearing crap up of Werewolf.<br /> B) All of the game lines are pretty heavily affected by your changes, and your changes actually show a preference towards the Garou's views of the universe. Insofar as their cosmology is the one that you utilize to the greatest extent.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96246#post96246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the distinction that you are trying to make between merely fixing and completely restructuring, but what you are missing is that the classic World of Darkness as a whole was just so deeply flawed logically that a sufficiently thorough &quot;fixing&quot; ends up being a complete restructuring. Deep flaws require equally deep corrections. If your fixing of the classic World of Darkness does not result in a complete restructuring, then you left at least one major contradiction unresolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said as much in my write-up.<br /> Rebuilding a house is not fixing its problems. It is admitting that its problems are too great to be fixed, and finding another route to eliminate them.<br /> I would also make a comparison to a broken leg. Sometimes you can re-set the bone. Sometimes the re-set isn't correct, or just doesn't heal correct, and you are left with something that still has flaws and isn't as good as it could be. And sometimes you need Automail.<br /> I did not miss this. I said this before. But the semantic distinction is still relevant.<br /> <br /> \u200bOver-all, if what you did works for you / your group, then great. I, personally, will do things like changing it so that Noddism isn't the cannon truth, and instead the first Vampire was a very unique and powerful Fomor if we are playing Werewolf. Or changing it so that the main reason the Crafts and Traditions have managed to survive for s long is because the TU is preoccupied with fighting everyone simultaneously (Changing Breeds, Vampires, and the Mystics) when playing Mage. Unless I am deliberately doing a restructuring, or else I know that the players will be encountering massively big-picture type stuff, I don't normally bother with the major cosmological changes, instead focusing only on the parts the characters interact with as necessary. Basically, I remember that the characters don't have a clue about that stuff, and it is meant to be a convoluted mess of unknowns to them, so it doesn't matter much to me what the universal truths are (again, unless it actually is relevant).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T12:13:31-07:00","id":96475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96246#post96246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was expecting that the lengthiest objection would come from a <i>Werewolf</i> fan, since the Garou are the most impacted by my proposed corrections.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can even call them &quot;corrections&quot;. You're homebrewing. You posted a hombrew setting. A lot of it doesn't exactly line up with the settings as they're written (Supernals aren't Primordials from Exalted and don't have world-bodies, for example). It's not the first time, and won't be the last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T17:35:31-07:00","id":96603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZhyzhaksMate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96382#post96382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not a fan of any one game line moreso than any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was your username and avatar that influenced my conclusion regarding what appeared to be your preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZhyzhaksMate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96382#post96382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I am deliberately doing a restructuring, or else I know that the players will be encountering massively big-picture type stuff, I don't normally bother with the major cosmological changes</div> </div> </div> </div>Massively big-picture stuff always impacts my players, sometimes in subtle ways that they don't fully notice right away. When they discover big-picture [metaphysical] truths and how those truths impact them and those around them, they can use and leverage that knowledge to their advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T09:28:57-07:00","id":96919,"title":"","content":"I think the issue with this version is that it sacrifices a lot of the flavour that makes the individual lines appealing for little real gain.<br /> <br /> Kindred aren't Wyrm-soldiers, they're tragic figures losing their humanity to the desperate need to stay in control/survive as monsters. Technocracy aren't static - they're about continual controlled changes to the consensus which makes them poor Weaver-soldiers and (leaving aside the Werewolves) the Lings don't really work as Wyld aligned because Seelie are bound by their word of honour, tradition and duty (Weaver static elements).<br /> <br /> The lines are a bit like siblings - they look enough like each other that people spot a resemblance, but they all have their own appeal and personality. If that gets sacrificed to &quot;fix&quot; them, that's not going to make the fans of any line happy nor be successful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T23:05:39-07:00","id":97314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The classic World of Darkness could not logically exist as it was described. To see this most clearly we simply look at the highest global powers. According to the classic </i><i>Vampire</i><i> game, elder vampires rule the world (as wielding entire nations as a personal resource is an Elder Background), but according to the classic </i><i>Mage</i><i> game, the Technocracy rules the world (as they supposedly control consensual reality itself). These two facts cannot coexist on a single planet, so what this really means is that THE fundamental power struggle in the classic World of Darkness would actually be vampires versus Technocrats; all of the supernatural beings in the World of Darkness would be affected by and drawn into this one core conflict of the global supernatural super powers.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think you are starting from a fundamentally flawed argument that the world doesn't work. What I think you are missing is the relationship between the Technocracy and most vampires. The Technocracy is waging a war for the beliefs of humanity. They do see vampires as well as any other supernatural creatures as &quot;Reality Deviants&quot; but on their long list of things to deal with vampires are pretty much at the bottom of it. <br /> <br /> &quot;Hmm...we have a group of extremely subtle Reality Deviants here, who not only are dedicated to staying out of the public eye, but in order to protect themselves will actively engage in propaganda to prevent humans from thinking about the supernatural elements they might see in the world. They have no interest in us or our activities and their activities night to night only benefit us. I think we'll kill them last.&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the elders of both the Camarilla and Sabbat look at the Technocracy something like this. I present two options below, the first is the more likely, the second is a more in depth option for those in a greater know.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mages? Are you kidding? Humans with magic powers who manipulate reality fighting for collective belief? Have you been feeding down at the drug clinic again?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Technocracy. We've encountered this organization before. They seem a great ally to the Masquerade, if for their own inscrutable reasons. Watch them closely and never trust them, but they seem a minor threat if any.&quot;<br /> <br /> Neither side really cares about the other in the long run. They can absolutely coexist because they aren't getting in each other's way.<br /> <br /> Pentex is another story, and really is getting in everyone's way. However Pentex is an unholy cross-sphere alliance of the worst elements of doom in the World of Darkness. I've seen used Pentex as antagonists in vampire (Cam and Sabbat), mage (Traditions and Technocracy), werewolf and KOE games, all quite successfully.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now if you want to establish a completely new world order (no pun intended) and completely rewrite 20 years of white wolf history for your games, go right ahead. But I would vehemently contest that this is necessary. Sure there are a few cracks (ok, sometimes more than a few), but your solution is like burning down the building and building a new one to fix a mold problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:14:37-07:00","id":97389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96919#post96919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue with this version is that it sacrifices a lot of the flavour that makes the individual lines appealing for little real gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gain&quot; is definitely subjective based on preferences. By creating a noncontradictory setting with an ubiquitous, cohesive metaphysic, I as a Storyteller gain a robust framework for enabling totally impromptu gamemastering; my players can be anything, go anywhere, and make any choice and I can readily generate answers to any questions their actions might invoke, without having to open a book to find an answer. This especially applies to exploration of mysteries of a mystical nature. What I gain is a flexibility to not have to try to cage my players into any prescribed plot; if they deviate from any plot, new plot arises readily from the consequences of their choices. Due to the finiteness of my attention, the only thing I really have to be concerned about enforcing on my players is just enough adhesion between them that I do not end up running a solo game for each player. Even my rules-lawyer who had page numbers in sourcebooks memorized found, after an adjustment period, that my &quot;big picture&quot; free-form gaming style engaged him in a way that previous games had not. Some people love freedom; others prefer to know the rules ahead of time. Again, the gain is subjective depending on the person. <br /> <br /> I guess I should note that I have never used the version of the World of Darkness with which I opened this thread; it's actually too confining for my tastes; it really was just an exercise in resolving contradictions. I employ a multiverse which is basically the Amber multiverse but with the dichotomy of Pattern and Logrus modified to be the trichotomy of the Triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:19:08-07:00","id":97393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97389#post97389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Gain&quot; is definitely subjective based on preferences. By creating a noncontradictory setting with an ubiquitous, cohesive metaphysic, I as a Storyteller gain a robust framework for enabling totally impromptu gamemastering; my players can be anything, go anywhere, and make any choice and I can readily generate answers to any questions their actions might invoke, without having to open a book to find an answer. This especially applies to exploration of mysteries of a mystical nature. What I gain is a flexibility to not have to try to cage my players into any prescribed plot; if they deviate from any plot, new plot arises readily from the consequences of their choices. Due to the finiteness of my attention, the only thing I really have to be concerned about enforcing on my players is just enough adhesion between them that I do not end up running a solo game for each player. Even my rules-lawyer who had page numbers in sourcebooks memorized found, after an adjustment period, that my &quot;big picture&quot; free-form gaming style engaged him in a way that previous games had not. Some people love freedom; others prefer to know the rules ahead of time. Again, the gain is subjective depending on the person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that these are all laudable goals for a game setting. I fail to see how all of this is not accomplished within the setting as written (with a few patches, but relatively minor ones).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T03:01:21-07:00","id":97416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97389#post97389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even my rules-lawyer who had page numbers in sourcebooks memorized found, after an adjustment period, that my &quot;big picture&quot; free-form gaming style engaged him in a way that previous games had not. Some people love freedom; others prefer to know the rules ahead of time. Again, the gain is subjective depending on the person.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, serious question:<br /> <br /> Why bother &quot;fixing&quot; the cWOD then?<br /> <br /> One of the nice things about there being lots of different games out there is that different games can appeal to different game styles. If the cWOD doesn't quite scratch the itch you want it to because of how the setting and metaplot have been established there are other options. The nWOD is, at least in terms of design, far more built towards the style of play you're describing. One of the big reasons I'm a fan of both lines is that they aren't same with slightly different rules. When I'm in the mood for the pre-defined setting, convoluted mess and all, I reach for the cWOD. When I'm in the mood for the toolkit of making the big picture whatever I want it to be, I'm going to reach for the nWOD.<br /> <br /> I think this gets to a lot of the push back against your idea. What you're proposing as a &quot;fix&quot; is basically removing the support for the play style that best aligns with the cWOD rather than looking for a game that hits the supported game style you seem to prefer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T06:42:04-07:00","id":97487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97393#post97393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see how all of this is not accomplished within the setting as written (with a few patches, but relatively minor ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you underestimate the impact of implementing a truly ubiquitous, cohesive metaphysic and mythology; the classic World of Darkness as written lacked such. Integrating just the Triat ubiquitously and taking it to its ultimate conclusions was no minor patch. Also, resolving the contradictions of the simultaneous existence of vampire elders, Technocracy, and Pentex as written is no small patch. To have two or more of them on the same planet, one or more of them must be scaled down from how they were written (at least when using the most hyperbolic versions of how they were written, such as the <i>Elders</i> sourcebook for <i>Vampire</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T06:50:14-07:00","id":97490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97416#post97416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why bother &quot;fixing&quot; the cWOD then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was motivated to resolve the contradictions in the classic World of Darkness because the Triat is my favorite pantheon of any fictional universe, because I am a geek who simply enjoyed the mental exercise of resolving the contradictions, and because I was curious to see if anyone one else had dramatic solutions to the contradictions (especially the bigger contradictions involving vampire elders, Technocracy, and/or Pentex).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T07:18:48-07:00","id":97500,"title":"","content":"My main criticism is that you're creating a problem that isn't actually there (the different worlds of darkness are actually separate), then you proceed to mash bits from different lines together and present it as your &quot;solution&quot;.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, I disagree with your basic premise as well as your execution.<br /> <br /> Whenever I want to do crossover, I always choose one line as the &quot;main&quot; and adapt everything else to fit into that paradigm. Makes for a heck of a lot less headaches, if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T07:49:11-07:00","id":97517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97389#post97389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Gain&quot; is definitely subjective based on preferences. By creating a noncontradictory setting with an ubiquitous, cohesive metaphysic, I as a Storyteller gain a robust framework for enabling totally impromptu gamemastering; my players can be anything, go anywhere, and make any choice and I can readily generate answers to any questions their actions might invoke, without having to open a book to find an answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing my point here - in science we use predictive power as a measure of how good an explanatory theory is. The more it fits the available data, the better the theory is. Treat your metaphysics rewrite as an explanatory theory and you'll see that it doesn't measure up. Its predictions drastically diverge from the established basic facts for each game line. Which means there's ~400-500 books of material which will be largely inconsistent with this explanation/rewrite and needs to be overhauled to fit. If you and your players enjoy it (or something like it), good for you, but you just need to look at the responses to this thread to see it's not really WoD to most people. :/<br /> <br /> If you really want to use the Triat to model the world, try picking out the member least associated with each supernatural. The intersection between the other two gives you more room to get a better fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 03-24-2014, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T10:22:05-07:00","id":97591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97487#post97487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you underestimate the impact of implementing a truly ubiquitous, cohesive metaphysic and mythology;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is underestimating the impact. The general sentiment of the disagreement is that the impact is more harm than benefit to the enjoyment of the cWOD for most groups.<br /> <br /> I've been playing and running the cWOD for just under 20 years. The vast majority of games I've been involved with (say ~85%) were single game-line. All the PCs were the same supernatural type, and the game was run with only books from that type mattering. The existence of other supernaturals was always twisted to benefit the metaphysics, cosmology, and mythology of the primary game being played. What is the positive impact of an over-arching WOD cohesiveness to that mode of play?<br /> <br /> The rest of the games that were not single supernatural-types only, were almost always either convention one-shots (which meant there was never time to worry about such things), or larger format games (LARPs, online play). With that second category, there is a very common response of downplaying the relevance/power of the &quot;global powers&quot; of the WOD. This isn't even about having PC vampires, werewolves, and mages (oh my!). It's about having so many PCs, and often a large disparity of power levels withing each group, that you need to loosen the grip on the upper levels of power for the older PCs to have space to occupy so they aren't crowding out the younger PCs for niches to fill. When you're part of running a game with 200+ PCs spread across most of the major game lines, with everything from mortals, to support (ghouls/kin/etc.), to full supernaturals represented, you tend to need to modify the game in a fashion that inherently downplays the cosmological differences rather than trying to remove them through unification. The VtM players don't want to get shoved into a different box, they want to play vampires/ghouls in VtM just with more other critters running around the city. You end up spending far more time addressing system contradictions than setting ones; because you can design the local setting to facilitate this mode of play more easily.<br /> <br /> So, again, where is the utility of this impact? To that mode of play, what does this unification actually add to the experience?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was motivated to resolve the contradictions in the classic World of Darkness because the Triat is my favorite pantheon of any fictional universe, because I am a geek who simply enjoyed the mental exercise of resolving the contradictions, and because I was curious to see if anyone one else had dramatic solutions to the contradictions (especially the bigger contradictions involving vampire elders, Technocracy, and/or Pentex). </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think any effort that starts with, &quot;this part of the metaphysical/cosmological setting of the WOD is my favorite,&quot; is going to end up shooting itself in the foot. It starts you off with a bias towards options that put your favorite thing front and center over options that would resolve any perceived contradictions with as little impact as possible.<br /> <br /> When you hamper yourself by putting forward, &quot;the Triat is now the grand metaphysical constant of the WOD,&quot; you end up adding work. The existence of Pentex, the Technocracy, and Elder vampires goes from something that either isn't actually a contradiction or a very minor patch (depending on your interpretation), into a huge effort because the Technocracy and the Elders were never designed to fit into the Triatic system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T14:51:26-07:00","id":97770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97500#post97500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main criticism is that you're creating a problem that isn't actually there (the different worlds of darkness are actually separate), then you proceed to mash bits from different lines together and present it as your &quot;solution&quot;.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, I disagree with your basic premise as well as your execution.<br /> <br /> Whenever I want to do crossover, I always choose one line as the &quot;main&quot; and adapt everything else to fit into that paradigm. Makes for a heck of a lot less headaches, if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1. Though I contest that the different worlds are separate. They are all part of the World of Darkness. The trick is to go into it with the understanding that no one has the answers entirely correct. Each sphere's mythology has elements of truth, but none are spot on (though I tend to think Demon has it the closest and usually base most of my cosmology on that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T17:18:02-07:00","id":97890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97770#post97770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I contest that the different worlds are separate. They are all part of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contest all you want. But as Heavy Arms pointed out already, if you crack up a 1e book, it's fairly clear that the intention was not for one united World of Darkness. It's still there in all the corebooks up to Revised, too, although by that time they'd caved and started giving more crossover rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T22:36:41-07:00","id":98098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97890#post97890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Contest all you want. But as Heavy Arms pointed out already, if you crack up a 1e book, it's fairly clear that the intention was not for one united World of Darkness. It's still there in all the corebooks up to Revised, too, although by that time they'd caved and started giving more crossover rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have opened up 1st edition books and they are littered with crossover. Just off the top of my head take a look at Dark Alliance: Vancouver (1992). An entirely crossover setting for Werewolf and Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T01:21:54-07:00","id":98190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97500#post97500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main criticism is that you're creating a problem that isn't actually there (the different worlds of darkness are actually separate)</div> </div> </div> </div>You are half right; in 1st Edition they were separate parallel Earths, then in 2nd Edition they sloppily [and inconsistently] tried to cram them all onto a single planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T01:30:21-07:00","id":98192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97517#post97517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're missing my point here - in science we use predictive power as a measure of how good an explanatory theory is. The more it fits the available data, the better the theory is. Treat your metaphysics rewrite as an explanatory theory and you'll see that it doesn't measure up. Its predictions drastically diverge from the established basic facts for each game line. Which means there's ~400-500 books of material which will be largely inconsistent with this explanation/rewrite and needs to be overhauled to fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yours is a paper tiger argument there, which misses the point of the exercise. My resolution of contradictions was not intended nor even implied to be predictive of the &quot;dataset&quot; of published facts. Indeed, my proposal very blatantly and unapologetically diverged from that contradictory mess of published &quot;facts&quot;. My proposal is really one thing and one thing only: a resolution of contradictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T01:55:04-07:00","id":98202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=98190#post98190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are half right; in 1st Edition they were separate parallel Earths, then in 2nd Edition they sloppily [and inconsistently] tried to cram them all onto a single planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, they still state the lines are in different worlds in the corebook. There simply was more published material, some of it crossovers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have opened up 1st edition books and they are littered with crossover. Just off the top of my head take a look at Dark Alliance: Vancouver (1992). An entirely crossover setting for Werewolf and Vampire. </div> </div> </div>According to the publishing lists, DA:Vancouver was published in 1993. That's after V:tM's 2nd edition and just one year prior to W:tA 2nd edition. So it's a nice find, but very likely one of the first crossovers, and saying more about the direction of 2e than 1e. As demonstrated by its, shall we say, rather unique take one the whole matter ? My memory of it is rather hazy, since I basically discarded it in disgust, but I seem to recall the different supernaturals working together in (relative) peace and harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T03:25:04-07:00","id":98236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=98192#post98192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yours is a paper tiger argument there, which misses the point of the exercise. My resolution of contradictions was not intended nor even implied to be predictive of the &quot;dataset&quot; of published facts. Indeed, my proposal very blatantly and unapologetically diverged from that contradictory mess of published &quot;facts&quot;. My proposal is really one thing and one thing only: a resolution of contradictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called giving the benefit of the doubt. A set of cohesive metaphysics is potentially useful, while arbitrarily chopping huge pieces off the setting is not. It's like someone gave you a jigsaw and your response was to cut bits off the pieces until they start to fit. It doesn't mean you've solved the jigsaw.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, your &quot;resolution of contradictions&quot; breaks several of the settings and creates many new contradictions (Kindred courts or Influence chess become bizarre things to be explained away rather than a function of Kindred desire to control/survive). If you pitched it as &quot;Triatworld - all Triat all the time&quot; rather than as a &quot;more logical World of Darkness&quot;, you'd find the reception would be different. As is, people are going to keep telling you that this is about as much a &quot;more logical World of Darkness&quot; as a banana is a &quot;curvy apple&quot;... :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 03-25-2014, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T06:20:00-07:00","id":98302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=98236#post98236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A set of cohesive metaphysics is potentially useful, while arbitrarily chopping huge pieces off the setting is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The arbitrary chopping off of pieces of the 2nd+ Edition cWoD setting is unavoidable though; every Storyteller had to do such because the World as described was just that disjointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T07:06:07-07:00","id":98323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=98302#post98302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The arbitrary chopping off of pieces of the 2nd+ Edition cWoD setting is unavoidable though; every Storyteller had to do such because the World as described was just that disjointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered that they're so contradictory because they were never meant to mix? Incidentally, there's recorded commentary from notable developers of the classic WoD games discussing how they were supposed to interrelate on DTRPG with the WW podcast, and they said, no, they were not really made with crossover explicitly in mind. Hence, not all one world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T07:47:35-07:00","id":98343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=98302#post98302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arbitrary chopping off of pieces of the 2nd+ Edition cWoD setting is unavoidable though; every Storyteller had to do such because the World as described was just that disjointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it as pruning a tree. Judicious pruning removes things that don't fit in to strengthen the overall shape of the tree and make the tree healthier. Over-pruning damages the tree. Triatworld doesn't look or act like WoD any longer- that's the issue. Take a look at this:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> - Camarilla do not make sense for these assumptions, Sabbat barely do (and don't work without the Camarilla). Many Clans cease to make sense<br /> <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b> - no new strength added to explanation. Many tribes cease to make sense (Glasswalkers, Silver Fangs nb here)<br /> <b>Mage: The Ascension </b>- not explained and Traditions/Technocracy conflict does not hold up with a full Weaver Technocracy (no consensus shifting).<br /> <b>Wraith: The Oblivion/Orpheus</b> - not explained.<br /> <b>Changeling: The Dreaming </b>- Seelie/Unseelie divide doesn't make sense nor does chimeric reality.<br /> <b>Kindred of the East</b> - not explained.<br /> <b>Hunter: The Reckoning</b> - not explained.<br /> <b>Mummy: The Resurrection </b>- not explained.<br /> <b>Demon: The Fallen </b> - not explained.<br /> <br /> You can see why I was talking about explanatory power earlier. It's not one or two pieces going awol or tossed out - it's the vast majority of the settings needing rewrites to function or to be scrapped because they do not fit this Triatworld motif.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I don't think all these games need center stage (and some of them I'm not fond of at all) but Triatworld bins most of what people see as oWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 03-25-2014, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T11:30:28-07:00","id":98503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97890#post97890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Contest all you want. But as Heavy Arms pointed out already, if you crack up a 1e book, it's fairly clear that the intention was not for one united World of Darkness. It's still there in all the corebooks up to Revised, too, although by that time they'd caved and started giving more crossover rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you got some page references on this, actually? Because my 1st Ed. books were pretty saturated with crossovers too. Hell, that's when Samuel Haight was the focal point of the metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T12:07:06-07:00","id":98547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=98302#post98302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">every Storyteller had to do such because the World as described was just that disjointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we didn't, because it only matters if you're worried about having the different game-lines co-exist in the game you're running.<br /> <br /> While I don't have any solid data one way or the other on this, my experience (as I detailed earlier) shows that this is not a major concern. Most Storytellers don't run cWOD with mixed supernatural groups and they don't care what Vampire says when they're running Mage, or what Changeling says when they're running Werewolf. The existence of other supernaturals are detailed in the logic and rules of the primary game being run because they're NPC that can be whatever the ST wants rather than the PC style characters from the other games that should then logically stay consistent with that game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T05:08:23-07:00","id":99065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97770#post97770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> +1. Though I contest that the different worlds are separate. They are all part of the World of Darkness. The trick is to go into it with the understanding that no one has the answers entirely correct. Each sphere's mythology has elements of truth, but none are spot on (though I tend to think Demon has it the closest and usually base most of my cosmology on that).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is much like how I approach things, but I'm a bit more Vampire-centric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T05:57:34-07:00","id":99090,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to note, Revised edition dialed back the gonzo madness of &quot;Oligarchus the Ventrue secretly controls the president!&quot; and Technocracy = Government (actually, this last one happened in latter 2nd Edition).<br /> <br /> That said, I've always ran all of the WoD lines separately, crossover-free (that are still Werewolves in my VtM, but they're not Garou and they don't fight against the Wyrm for Gaia). IMO, a unified cosmology (even the &quot;all of them are true!&quot; thing from Demon) doesn't do much for the game itself beyond the forum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T09:33:09-07:00","id":99231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=96475#post96475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're homebrewing. You posted a hombrew setting. A lot of it doesn't exactly line up with the settings as they're written (Supernals aren't Primordials from Exalted and don't have world-bodies, for example). It's not the first time, and won't be the last.</div> </div> </div> </div> They way I see it, running a game with true crossover metaphysics and mythos militates that one homebrew. Running a V:tM game with some mage stuff doesn't really require homebrew because you can just use the V:tM explanations for everything (the same goes for running a game based explicitly on one line with cameos by other lines). However, the moment that you decide that you want to have parity between the respective mythos of two lines, you <i>must</i> homebrew.<br /> <br /> That said, once one has undertaken the task of cobbling together a homebrew cWoD cosmology, I think a great deal can be achieved or accomplished by treating the setting material for each respective game as having been written by an unreliable narrator. The Triat of W:tA and the cosmological forces of Stasis, Dynamism, and Entropy that feature in M:tAs, can be the same thing, but simply experienced or characterized differently by those two groups. The phenomena themselves are abstract and <i>out there</i> enough that it doesn't seem like too much of a stretch. If you want to incorporate Vampire, Demon (and I guess Hunter), then you declare that, absolutely above <i>everything</i> in the universe that is even remotely knowable, there is the Abrahamic deity, 'God'. So on and so forth.<br /> <br /> I've been playing these games for about 16 years now (mostly Storytelling though), and I've run nigh the same cosmology for the majority of it -- and I've found that I can give almost equal deference to all the game lines' respective mythos without need to drastically change the character of any given entity (like making Pentex a solely vampiric undertaking or something). Furthermore, unless you're running a super high-level game, a great deal of the harder inconsistencies to smooth over don't actually need to be addressed in the game, as they're of such a cosmological character that the players are unlikely to ever be forced to deal with a problem that requires clear explanations as to what is and isn't <i>the truth</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T11:50:45-07:00","id":99362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>romanov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=99090#post99090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanted to note, Revised edition dialed back the gonzo madness of &quot;Oligarchus the Ventrue secretly controls the president!&quot; and Technocracy = Government (actually, this last one happened in latter 2nd Edition).<br /> <br /> That said, I've always ran all of the WoD lines separately, crossover-free (that are still Werewolves in my VtM, but they're not Garou and they don't fight against the Wyrm for Gaia). IMO, a unified cosmology (even the &quot;all of them are true!&quot; thing from Demon) doesn't do much for the game itself beyond the forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are of course free to run your games how you like, but I would never want to run WoD without it being a complete world. That glorious mess is what I love about it. I've played in games where the ST tried to fake the other spheres without really using them and it just felt empty to me. <br /> <br /> The only thing I will contest is the statement that you <i>cannot</i> run a complete world of darkness. I do so with every game I run. It takes few patches on the worst spots of contradictions and a few creative interpretations but overall it works fantastically well. If you don't wan to, that's between you and your players. But there is nothing stopping it, and I'd encourage those who haven't tried it yet to at least make the attempt. I think your games will be richer for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:36:16-07:00","id":101690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=97591#post97591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been playing and running the cWOD for just under 20 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, respect.<br /> <br /> But OT: Yeah, essentially what you're doing is just making up your own setting to suit your tastes. Good for you, hope you have fun with it and it works out. But logic has never played a huge role in WoD: if things were logical, then they'd be explainable, which'd (at least for me) take away a little from the sheer unknowable-brain-screw that it is. It's like that One Player who feels the need to mechanicalise or identify every thing you throw in, that objects if you interpret the wording of a Discipline or spell or whatever a little liberally in order for awesome or narrative necessity. The WoD is full of just weird crap, and has a fairly large &quot;Misc&quot; folder, and seemingly contradictory realities are just more of that.<br /> <br /> If you want to make up your own setting where everything is explainable and &quot;logical&quot;, then go ahead. As stated before, I hope it works out for you. But I think you might be playing the wrong game if that's what you want. Try Shadowrun, that's pretty logical (I think?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T01:43:38-07:00","id":109097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=98323#post98323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered that they're so contradictory because they were never meant to mix?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that that is exactly where the contradictions come from. Some developers developed as if the worlds were separate, but other developers developed for a single crowded planet. The lack of consistent central supervision resulted in neither entirely separate worlds nor an entirely unified world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T13:05:52-07:00","id":111013,"title":"","content":"The wod very much works as it is. I consider the different cosmologies as merely different interpretations of similar phenomena and in regards to power structures. Well most Vampires(yes even fearsome Elders) will never know or care about the Technocracy, the ones who do fear them and the ones who do and try to find out more or hunt them will have serious problems whether it's their mind wiped or their existence corrected. The Technocracy doesn't care all that much at competing with Vampires, their masquerade is actually a good thing and Pentex doesn't clash with Vampires either, also as extensively discussed throughout this thread the influence structures are loose and not usually so direct.<br /> <br /> You can of course make a crazy world where the vampires are knights in service of the wyrm but justifying it on the basis that the default wod doesn't work when it has worked for over 20 years is not a good start imo. There are multiple crossover chronicles even in revised. I think the divide is much more mechanical if anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>former lightmaguz","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/514-auron","name":"Auron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T13:19:47-07:00","id":111026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Auron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=111013#post111013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wod very much works as it is. I consider the different cosmologies as merely different interpretations of similar phenomena and in regards to power structures. Well most Vampires(yes even fearsome Elders) will never know or care about the Technocracy, the ones who do fear them and the ones who do and try to find out more or hunt them will have serious problems whether it's their mind wiped or their existence corrected. The Technocracy doesn't care all that much at competing with Vampires, their masquerade is actually a good thing and Pentex doesn't clash with Vampires either, also as extensively discussed throughout this thread the influence structures are loose and not usually so direct.<br /> <br /> You can of course make a crazy world where the vampires are knights in service of the wyrm but justifying it on the basis that the default wod doesn't work when it has worked for over 20 years is not a good start imo. There are multiple crossover chronicles even in revised. I think the divide is much more mechanical if anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that's not about interpretation - the Umbra in Mage is not the same Umbra in Werewolf. The former has space as a place you go with the Spirit Sphere and refers to abstract realms as being part of the High Umbra. The latter has space as a place you go to with rocketry and refers to abstract realms as being part of the Deep Umbra. There's a Gauntlet in space that's thin, but still distinct.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T17:43:50-07:00","id":111141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=111026#post111026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something that's not about interpretation - the Umbra in Mage is not the same Umbra in Werewolf. The former has space as a place you go with the Spirit Sphere and refers to abstract realms as being part of the High Umbra. The latter has space as a place you go to with rocketry and refers to abstract realms as being part of the Deep Umbra. There's a Gauntlet in space that's thin, but still distinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is solvable simply enough by saying any and all are true...at least in part. The Umbra is the hardest part of cosmology to unify but, I've managed to run campaigns involving the Umbra crossing over with vampires, mages and werwolves in the party. <br /> <br /> As for the differing theologies, the answer is incredibly simple. No one is entirely right. Every sphere presents their own theories but no one (Demon included, though I usually run them as the closest to right) have all the answers. Each is looking at the world through their own lens. This is why you see so many strange similarities in the mythologies (take a look at the two brothers story from Changeling and how close that is to the Abrahamic Caine and Abel story used in Vampire) with different interpretations. I've got theories as to the overall truth which takes elements from all of them but takes none of them as absolute canon, but I shift these as needed per game and it works well enough. There is absolutely no need to put everyone on the same page, and I think it strips a great deal of flavour out of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T13:36:06-07:00","id":112911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=95532#post95532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No vampire on the planet can just call up the White House, say &quot;Hey, invade Panama for me will ya?&quot; and have it happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, in the <i>Vampire</i> sourcebooks various wars throughout history are explained as the result of warring vampire Clans. The <i>Influence</i> Background in the <i>Elders</i> sourcebook does indeed give vampire elders the frightening level of control and power to be able to wield an entire nation's army against a rival elder's army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T05:59:47-07:00","id":113279,"title":"","content":"Really? Your justification for completely rewriting the world is one background in a 2nd edition book in a section that has largely been disowned for its sheer ridiculousness (I mean really, generation controlling backgrounds)? You'll have to do better than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T07:26:50-07:00","id":113311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=112911#post112911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, in the <i>Vampire</i> sourcebooks various wars throughout history are explained as the result of warring vampire Clans. The <i>Influence</i> Background in the <i>Elders</i> sourcebook does indeed give vampire elders the frightening level of control and power to be able to wield an entire nation's army against a rival elder's army.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Wolfgar's point stands. You're taking one bit out of context (provided below). Vampire's influence not control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=95532#post95532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire elders <i>control</i> very little. What they do is <i>influence</i>, which is quite different. No vampire on the planet can just call up the White House, say &quot;Hey, invade Panama for me will ya?&quot; and have it happen. It doesn't work like that. It's like a guy pushing a car. Sure, he has some impact on what direction the car goes, but the weight of the car and the shape of the road are bigger forces. It's still ridiculously impressive compared to most of us - we would be ants trying to the car - but true control is impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Wolfgar is describing is pretty clearly what the Influence background does. It (including the extra 6-10 levels provided in Elysium: the Elder wars) represents having minions and compromised agents spread throughout areas of interest (in the Elysium levels you're talking about minions spread throughout important systems worldwide). These minions may attempt to influence policy towards any end you want - but they're still putting themselves on the chopping block whenever they do so.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, any of these attempts within the Influence levels an Elder has allows them to make a Manipulation+Influence roll against the ST. The impact of successes and the difficulty of the task are ST determined. So, taking 'call up the White House, say &quot;Hey, invade Panama for me will ya?&quot; and have it happen' as the overall aim and methodology, you might have the following set up:<br /> <br /> Difficulty 10. 9 if ST is feeling generous (this is about as risky an implementation as is possible)<br /> Botch: Watergate 2 and Elder is in danger (odds are about as good as getting a single success at 10 and a nontrivial outcome for difficulty 9).<br /> Success 1: US relations with Panama become strained.<br /> Success 2: US withdraws from cooperative policies with Panama.<br /> Success 3: US relations with Panama become hostile.<br /> Success 4: US comes to the brink of war with Panama. War is likely but not inevitable.<br /> Success 5: US Invades Panama right this second.<br /> <br /> So the Elder might have the minions in place to escalate or diminish an existing conflict (at a risk to themselves) but they pretty much can't 'call up the White House, say &quot;Hey, invade Panama for me will ya?&quot; and have it happen.' ... unless the ST doesn't understand how to set difficulty and successes and/or the static risk-averse Elder is willing to throw away everything on a literal roll of the dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 04-15-2014, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T01:50:57-07:00","id":114611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=113279#post113279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your justification for completely rewriting the world is one background in a 2nd edition book in a section that has largely been disowned for its sheer ridiculousness</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be conveniently forgetting all of the other references throughout various <i>Vampire</i> books which paint them as the secret masters of the world since antiquity. The Background I cited was merely the most overt example. You may have chosen to dismiss the notion of vampires as secret masters as not fitting to your personal take on the World of Darkness, but that does not change the fact that vampiric global mastery is part of the published canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T01:56:52-07:00","id":114614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=113311#post113311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically speaking, any of these attempts within the Influence levels an Elder has allows them to make a Manipulation+Influence roll against the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was there more than one edition of that sourcebook? The Background that I remember was for Storytellers to model their NPC elders according to the &quot;secret masters theory&quot;, not for player-characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T03:02:36-07:00","id":114631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=114614#post114614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was there more than one edition of that sourcebook? The Background that I remember was for Storytellers to model their NPC elders according to the &quot;secret masters theory&quot;, not for player-characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a MET version (Laws of Elysium) and Elysium: The Elder wars which was reprinted twice (once in War of Ages). In general Elysium is an Elder character supplement - so designed for use by STs and players in Elder campaigns.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;Secret Master Theory&quot; stuff. I think you've a disconnect between your image of Masquerade and what the setting is about. Masquerade as a setting has its roots in the 13th century where the &quot;Dark Ages Vampire&quot; setting begins to crumble as the mortals rise up against the semi-open Vampires (the Spanish Inquisition) and the disaffected childer rebel.<br /> <br /> In the 15th century, a coterie of powerful Vampires is able to form an organization which gets the lid back on the pressure cooker and tries to hold it there. Those Vampires are the Founders, that organization is the Camarilla and the stricture about never being found out again is the titular Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Jump forward to the modern day. Kindred society is now based on behind the scenes influence rather than outright control. Kindred &quot;secret mastering&quot; is limited to subtle things that can be pawned off as corruption etc. because the society as a whole can't afford to be found out - which means penalties for breaching the Masquerade are extremely harsh.<br /> <br /> In other words, they can push an anti-panama agenda slowly over time if they really need to (get the right candidate elected/blackmail someone low on the totem pole) but invading Panama without a reason is right out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 04-17-2014, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T01:53:30-07:00","id":120842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=114631#post114631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Masquerade as a setting has its roots in the 13th century where the &quot;Dark Ages Vampire&quot; setting begins to crumble..</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Masquerade as a setting element has its roots as a simple literary technique. When the idea of the Masquerade was first published it had no published in-world origin, and the <i>Dark Ages</i> game line and all of its explanations had not even been conceived yet. The Masquerade as a setting element began as a simple literary technique for enabling powerful supernatural beings to exist in a world that sufficiently resembled our own on the surface. Note that the vampires' Masquerade served the same literary function as the werewolves' Delirium; what differentiated the Masquerade from the Delirium is that the Masquerade began as a generic &quot;secret masters theory&quot;, whereas the Delirium operated as a supernatural effect. Some White Wolf authors then later extrapolated upon that generic &quot;secret masters theory&quot; in various permutations, not all of them being entirely compatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T03:33:25-07:00","id":120868,"title":"","content":"The origin has been the case since first ed. The DA setting wasn't detailed at that point but the &quot;time before the Inquisition&quot; was.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure what you're trying to achieve at this point tbh. You seem to be snipping people's posts to find things to argue over. Let it go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T02:03:56-07:00","id":124359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=120868#post120868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be snipping people's posts to find things to argue over.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other times and places I've had discussions about the deep contradictions in the classic World of Darkness and heard intriguing, grandiose, sometimes world-changing resolutions; I was hoping to repeat that here. I had predicted that Werewolf fans such as yourself would be the most vocal in objecting to my particular set of resolutions; what I did not predict was that no one in this Onyx Path forum would have grandiose world-changing resolutions to share. I guess I am unique in that where the other critics against the contradictions apparently moved on to other games (or to, gasp, Real Life), my love of the Triat pantheon adhered me to remain. In the absence of alternative world-changing resolutions in this thread, mostly what I ended up with was Werewolf fans wanting to downplay the power of vampiric elders. (Oh, and the multiple-worlds-versus-single-world debate that I entirely failed to predict; in my meatspace circles the &quot;contradictory single world&quot; was a given.) The Werewolf fans voted with their posts for this thread to be a debate, so I have been playing along; I simply don't have the time though to respond to every statement made by every poster, so I have to pick and choose. Besides, if everyone thought and felt identically, there would be nothing to discuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T05:04:08-07:00","id":124415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=124359#post124359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other times and places I've had discussions about the deep contradictions in the classic World of Darkness and heard intriguing, grandiose, sometimes world-changing resolutions; I was hoping to repeat that here.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's silly. Either you're just going to repeat a conversation you've already had, or you're going to not get the same conversations you had the in the past.<br /> <br /> What's the point of the first? And why would you expect the second to result in the same as the first?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had predicted that Werewolf fans such as yourself would be the most vocal in objecting to my particular set of resolutions </div> </div> </div>This puts your first statement in serious doubt. Having a preconceived bias against fans of a specific game-line is explicitly counter-productive to your stated objective.<br /> <br /> As well, your passive-aggressive snide remarks do nothing but make Obyrne's statement look more likely to be true. Using a WtA themed handle and/or avatar pic to label and dismiss someone as a WtA fan is actively detrimental to the conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...what I did not predict was that no one in this Onyx Path forum would have grandiose world-changing resolutions to share. </div> </div> </div>Well, there you go. Now you know that the vocal people on this forum aren't particularly keen on this thought exercise. Though as previously mentioned, your phrasing and presentation of your premise were flawed. Your posting has not being successful, stylistically, at steering the conversation towards, &quot;grandiose world-changing&quot; alterations to the cWOD setting. Instead it started, and has remained, as an analysis of your particular attempt at such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess I am unique in that where the other critics against the contradictions apparently moved on to other games (or to, gasp, Real Life), my love of the Triat pantheon adhered me to remain. </div> </div> </div>No, you're not unique. It's just that the critics either learned to live with them and how to make small alterations more often or moved on; than chose to worry about grandiose fixes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T10:49:11-07:00","id":124603,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've never been a big fan of crossovers. Not because of inconsistencies between the systems or the setting (some degree of suspension of disbelief is required) so much as the settings' individual flavors are often compromised when you try to combine them. I find that Vampire in particular suffers from being crossed with other setting and my personal preference isn't to have other supernatural creatures in a Vampire game at all, much less their cosmologies, aside perhaps from a rumor or legend here or there. Vampire, for me, is a game of vampire vs vampire, vampire vs mortal, and vampire vs self - throwing a bunch of werewolves or mages into that mix throws things off.<br /> <br /> In a Mage game, I like for the Technology to dominate much of the political landscape, having to deal with Pentex or vampires getting in the way. The same thing goes for elder vampires in V:tM and Pentex in W:tA.<br /> <br /> I also think that many of the deep cosmological issues don't have to be answered. When I am running a V:tM game, I don't need to decide if Caine exists or if the Wyrm created the Antediluvians - the characters are never going to know the truth of that, neither should the players, and actually the ST doesn't need to know either. I think that keeping things mysterious is the best option for both crossover and non-crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 05-03-2014, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T23:19:29-07:00","id":128774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=124415#post124415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's silly. Either you're just going to repeat a conversation you've already had, or you're going to not get the same conversations you had the in the past. What's the point of the first? And why would you expect the second to result in the same as the first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your spurious logic there is based on the flawed presumption that no one in this Onyx Path forum is creative enough to surprise me with a grandiose resolution that I have not heard in prior conversations. I know that you do not actually have such a low opinion of your fellow Onyx Path forum posters, so from that I can only conclude that your post is flamebait. Skimming the rest of your post, I only see more such spurious logic and flamebaiting.<br /> <br /> Great, now you've sucked me into competing in the Special Olympics with you. Once a discussion devolves into flamebaiting it's just a tragic farce at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2509,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","user":"Thanateros","date":". 05-09-2014, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T00:22:35-07:00","id":128793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=124603#post124603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that many of the deep cosmological issues don't have to be answered. When I am running a V:tM game, I don't need to decide if Caine exists or if the Wyrm created the Antediluvians - the characters are never going to know the truth of that, neither should the players, and actually the ST doesn't need to know either. I think that keeping things mysterious is the best option for both crossover and non-crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a player, I deeply appreciate a mystery with enough depth of forethought for me to actually be able to explore and uncover it. As a Storyteller I like to provide that opportunity of depth to my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T00:45:38-07:00","id":128799,"title":"","content":"I'm often baffled by my players' lack of apparent interest in the deeper metaplot structures. With a few notable exceptions, my players are happy enough just skimming the surface of things. Of course, that doesn't keep me from knowing what each and every Antediluvian, Incarna, Marauder and Spectre is up to - or what they each had for breakfast that day. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T00:56:19-07:00","id":128802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=128774#post128774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your spurious logic there is based on the flawed presumption that no one in this Onyx Path forum is creative enough to surprise me with a grandiose resolution that I have not heard in prior conversations.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. My logic assumes that the posters here are not the same as the people you've already had this conversation with. That's all.<br /> <br /> This does mean that it is a distinct possibility that nobody here will surprise you with a grandiose resolution that you have not heard in a prior conversation. Even if people were generally inclined to post grandiose resolutions along the thought experiment you proposed (poorly), they could easily fail to surprise you. We don't have a comprehensive list of what you've already heard. It's very simple to assume that two separate groups of creative people, starting with the same base inspiration and doing the same thought experiment end up creating a large quantity of overlapping results.<br /> <br /> You notice how this doesn't involve insulting anybody?<br /> <br /> And your outrage is a nice, but transparent, side-step from my point: if you came here to have a conversation and were hoping to get new responses that you haven't seen before then there's no point in getting upset, demeaning, or aggressive when you get results that differ from your past experiences. That is, after all, why you started the conversation again. Just because this instance of that conversation did not generate data useful to you isn't our fault.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that you do not actually have such a low opinion of your fellow Onyx Path forum posters, so from that I can only conclude that your post is flamebait. </div> </div> </div>Nice spurious logic there. Shall I list the massive number of logically pitfalls this single sentence exemplifies?<br /> <br /> You can conclude a lot of other things from my post other than that actually. For example:<br /> <br /> 1) I'm trying to point out to you that your posts do not serve the purpose of spurring forumites to engage in your thought exercise. Instead of asking people for ideas, you simply presented your idea. So people picked apart your idea without presenting their own. Because you never asked. If your goal was to have a thread of grandiose alterations to the cWOD setting with an eye towards greater internal logical consistency, then you need to actually pose the question to the community at some point.<br /> <br /> 2) I'm trying to point out to you that dismissing fans of a particular game-line out of hand is poor form. As well, labeling anyone with a handle/avatar related to that line as a fan of that line specifically and then dismissing them is also poor form.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm trying to point out to you that the stylistic choices you've made in your posts are at odds with your stated desires and interests in terms of responses.<br /> <br /> Notice, none of those are flamewar topics. None of those should be flamebait. Everything there is, while negative, actual constructive criticism that you could think over, and perhaps apply to this and future threads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Skimming the rest of your post, I only see more such spurious logic and flamebaiting.<br /> <br /> Great, now you've sucked me into competing in the Special Olympics with you. Once a discussion devolves into flamebaiting it's just a tragic farce at that point. </div> </div> </div>You keep using these words. I do not think they mean what you think they mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a player, I deeply appreciate a mystery with enough depth of forethought for me to actually be able to explore and uncover it. As a Storyteller I like to provide that opportunity of depth to my players. </div> </div> </div>These are not mutually exclusive things. A setting can have unsolvable deep mysteries about the fundamental nature of reality, while also having deep mysteries that are entirely solvable.<br /> <br /> For example, you don't need to have Caine be a solvable mystery to have the full history of the Black Hand be a solvable mystery for the players to explore and uncover.<br /> <br /> There's also the factor of the more &quot;answered&quot; mysteries are detailed in the books, the less enjoyment there is in exploring them because those are set. A setting with lots of undefined mysteries leave the ST free to create new answers every time, so that even if you played exploring the true history of Caine and the origin of vampires you could have a unique, engaging, and fun mystery each time because there isn't a set answer everyone knows is waiting at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T04:06:00-07:00","id":136508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=124359#post124359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess I am unique in that where the other critics against the contradictions apparently moved on to other games (or to, gasp, Real Life),</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll quote that whenever someone asks me what's special snowflake syndrome...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>former lightmaguz","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/514-auron","name":"Auron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T05:37:45-07:00","id":139213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=128802#post128802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...if you came here to have a conversation and were hoping to get new responses that you haven't seen before then there's no point in getting upset, demeaning, or aggressive when you get results that differ from your past experiences. I'm trying to point out to you that dismissing fans of a particular game-line out of hand is poor form.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep misconstruing my prediction about objections from <i>Werewolf</i> fans as somehow being an insult against them. My resolutions subjectively &quot;reduced&quot; werewolves into &quot;werepookas&quot; so to speak, which admittedly destroys the published flavor of <i>Werewolf</i>, so it is perfectly reasonable and expected for <i>Werewolf</i> fans to seek to dismantle such. A simple prediction about such objections is neither a dismissal nor an insult. (Personally, I love the idea of chimerical beasts out of nightmares.) <br /> <br /> Let's talk about actual insults...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=124359#post124359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I am unique in that where the other critics against the contradictions apparently moved on to other games (or to, gasp, Real Life), my love of the Triat pantheon adhered me to remain.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=124415#post124415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you're not unique.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Auron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=136508#post136508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll quote that whenever someone asks me what's special snowflake syndrome...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf I had phrased that as &quot;I guess I am the oddball in that...&quot;, no one would have jumped to tear down a [nonexistent] boast of &quot;specialness&quot;. My use of the word &quot;unique&quot; as merely a numeric adjective was obvious; Heavy Arms' use of &quot;unique&quot; was as a qualitative adjective, which makes a statement like &quot;No, you're not unique&quot; nothing other than blatant degradation. <br /> <br /> Even if someone were to boast, warranted or unwarranted, a blatantly degrading statement like that is still inappropriate. That fact that people do jump to tear down simple use of a word like &quot;unique&quot; does not speak well of the culture here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T05:50:56-07:00","id":139217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=128802#post128802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to point out to you that your posts do not serve the purpose of spurring forumites to engage in your thought exercise. Instead of asking people for ideas, you simply presented your idea. So people picked apart your idea without presenting their own. Because you never asked. If your goal was to have a thread of grandiose alterations to the cWOD setting with an eye towards greater internal logical consistency, then you need to actually pose the question to the community at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good point there. In past conversations I never had to explicitly ask; indeed, eager fellow Storytellers would sometimes interrupt me to volunteer their own homebrewed solutions. I was [mistakenly] expecting the same level of eager &quot;volunteerism&quot; here. If I had the option to delete this entire thread, I would start a new thread with a such a question, and my set of resolutions would be the first reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:33:24-07:00","id":139248,"title":"","content":"Well, your tone is pretty horrible and you're an obvious elitist. I would guess you are still somewhat young, as that tends to come with the territory.<br /> <br /> That being said, I will say that for almost 20 years I have ST in a complete cross-over world that included all five main lines. The biggest change I made was to &quot;population&quot; of supernaturals... as I wanted my world to still be very mortal-driven.<br /> <br /> I use Mage metaphysics as my base, and in doing so it is very easy to extend the differences between each of the factions and the way they see the universe to different venues and the way they might.<br /> <br /> It really isn't that complicated, and contradictions are actually very few and far between. Maybe this is because I dealt with them so long ago.<br /> <br /> Like others have said, what you have here is a homebrew. That's great and all... but your tone is basically &quot;if you can't see why MY homebrew is better than the canon, you just aren't on my level&quot;. What people here are saying is that your solutions go way too far, and with a bit more analysis and subtlety you could accomplish the end goal of a full cross-over game. We know this because we have been doing it for years - some of us decades.<br /> <br /> You are presumptuous and it seems like you want agreement more than discussion. I don't mean this in a disparaging way, but rather as an honest perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T20:13:41-07:00","id":140178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=128793#post128793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a player, I deeply appreciate a mystery with enough depth of forethought for me to actually be able to explore and uncover it. As a Storyteller I like to provide that opportunity of depth to my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> OK, with that in mind, I'll respond a bit to your original post.<br /> <br /> I think if you're going to have vampires as the power behind Pentex, you might as well ditch Pentex entirely. There is no need for it, merely emphasize the vast influence of ancient vampires and the nature of that influence. Elder vampires use their power to expand the cities, to create poverty and crime so that they can more easy feed, are corrupt and manipulative. The Tzimisce create ghouls that are as frightening as Formori and do things as evil as what the BSD's do. You could still have the BSD's and banes, but instead of Pentex just present vampires in all their wickedness - from the manipulative corrupt elders of the Camarilla to the insane and violent Sabbat. Of course, if you do this it will heavily alter things from the vampire side of the equation - because vampires' primary enemy has traditionally been each other but if you redesign the setting in this way and want it to be consistent for all game lines, werewolves will be a major factor in vampire politics and relations.<br /> <br /> Mages would also be bigger enemies to Garou, with the Nephandi being major villains to them and allies to the BSD and Wyrm spirits, and the Technocracy pushing for more and more Weaver dominance, expansion of cities, increased technology, and so on. <br /> <br /> This all seems to me of having the effect of making the other game lines more like Werewolf - with epic battles between warring factions with no common ground instead of the more subtle intrigues that might dominate mage conflict and especially that of vampires. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T01:18:28-07:00","id":140332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=139213#post139213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You keep misconstruing my prediction about objections from <i>Werewolf</i> fans as somehow being an insult against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your predictions <i>are</i> insults against them. They're prejudice it its most fundamental form. You are pre-judging a group of people based on your stereotyped assumptions about them.<br /> <br /> I'm also speaking rather directly about two specific things you said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was expecting that the lengthiest objection would come from a <i>Werewolf</i> fan, since the Garou are the most impacted by my proposed corrections. </div> </div> </div>Which was a direct response to ZhyzhaksMate's post which... was not at all about the specific changes you made to the Garou. This wasn't so bad.. but it was only one statement at the beginning of the thread. This though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Werewolf fans voted with their posts for this thread to be a debate, so I have been playing along; </div> </div> </div>Crossed the line for me. I can come up with no generous reading of this line that isn't dumping on WtA fans here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My resolutions subjectively &quot;reduced&quot; werewolves into &quot;werepookas&quot; so to speak, which admittedly destroys the published flavor of <i>Werewolf</i>, so it is perfectly reasonable and expected for <i>Werewolf</i> fans to seek to dismantle such. A simple prediction about such objections is neither a dismissal nor an insult. </div> </div> </div>Where, exactly, did anyone post this specific complaint? Because a lot of us voiced this much more as your proposal destroying the published flavor of <i>the entire classic World of Darkness</i>. Not just one game line. And that's why focusing on the &quot;boogeyman&quot; of WtA fans is dismissive and insulting; even if you did not intend to be such.<br /> <br /> And that's something I don't feel you're quite getting about this. You don't have to mean to be insulting to offend someone. You don't have to mean to be dismissive to make someone feel ignored.<br /> <br /> That way you are choosing to phrase things here though? They are causing that effect. And since we are not psychic, we have to go on what words you use, not what you mean in your head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bIf I had phrased that as &quot;I guess I am the oddball in that...&quot;, no one would have jumped to tear down a [nonexistent] boast of &quot;specialness&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Nope. I might have altered my phrasing but either way your post would have still come off as you trying to use the general lack of support for your posts to prop yourself up. Again, your intent to come off as a special snowflake not actually existing doesn't change how your post said, &quot;I'm a special snowflake.&quot; Whipping out the thesaurus to come up with different words wouldn't have changed it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My use of the word &quot;unique&quot; as merely a numeric adjective was obvious; Heavy Arms' use of &quot;unique&quot; was as a qualitative adjective, which makes a statement like &quot;No, you're not unique&quot; nothing other than blatant degradation. </div> </div> </div>And you're playing the special snowflake card again, even if you don't mean it.<br /> <br /> Look at what you're saying. You're claiming that your statement was so obvious (a skill that means you must be a very special person to actually assume is the case) that any misinterpretation of it must be malicious instead of accidental.<br /> <br /> And... I didn't mean &quot;unique&quot; qualitatively. I meant it quantitatively, because you know it actually isn't true. You have said, directly, have you know other people that have shared your enthusiasm for this thought exercise. So either you know that you are not unique in this, or you aren't telling the truth about knowing other people that share your interest. I chose to interpret your statement under the assumption that you are not being purposefully misleading.<br /> <br /> As well, as I've been saying, you really don't know how many posters here would like to help build/come up with their own &quot;Triat World&quot; homebrews of the WOD. As you concede, you didn't approach this well from your first post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That fact that people do jump to tear down simple use of a word like &quot;unique&quot; does not speak well of the culture here. </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to assume you're young... but this strikes me as the comment of someone that is not used to forums and similar Internet discussion mediums.<br /> <br /> This is not a unique phenomenon to this forum. You will find distaste for that sort of line across the Internet because there are reasons why phrases like &quot;special snowflake syndrome&quot; exist. Most of us have, realistically, been there. We start in a small tight-knit interpersonal group around a niche hobby where we are unique (in either sense) for good or ill. We find a huge community of thousands of people on the Internet seeking validation of ideas we thought were original or awesome or whatever and then... we get hit with the fact that in this larger community we're not all that unique and special. Most of the ideas we had, someone else had too. Most of the debates we thought were unsettled have long since been beaten to death.<br /> <br /> I remember my first Mage flame war... oh 15 years ago I think? In my TT group I was the Mage guru. I knew all the books inside and out. I could weave all the odd disparities together into one unified vision with a few paragraphs of awesome... and boy did I get shut down hard. People, literally, had copy &amp; paste responses to tear apart everything I jumped into my first thread with. It sucked, they were vicious,... but I was also naive as shit to think that. For them it was dead horse revisted #12324 and they didn't have any reason to not let me know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You make a good point there. In past conversations I never had to explicitly ask; indeed, eager fellow Storytellers would sometimes interrupt me to volunteer their own homebrewed solutions. </div> </div> </div>Again, this reinforces my assumption that you're kinda new to forums. We can't interrupt each other here. It's also really hard to relate tonal things like &quot;excitement&quot; and &quot;eagerness.&quot; And as this thread well illustrates, humans tend towards filling in tonal blanks with negativity.<br /> <br /> Forum conversations have a flow and style all their own. They don't work like sitting around your living room shooting the shit and having complete geek-outs about someone everyone there loves (which is awesome, I kinda miss that happening as much for my as it used to).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I had the option to delete this entire thread, I would start a new thread with a such a question, and my set of resolutions would be the first reply. </div> </div> </div>Cool. For all that's been said, I do kind of look forward to you trying something similar (since this topic is kinda shot) with this mindset. Lets see what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T07:47:08-07:00","id":143433,"title":"","content":"I like the premise of Changeling: The Lost more. Is it feasible to just ignore the Dreaming and replace it with the Lost in one's cWoD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T22:33:56-07:00","id":146385,"title":"","content":"too be honest there was never a problem with me in the inconsistencies between cosmologies. every critter in the cWOD is just like any other religion or belief system in the real world. they don't have to be compatible to co exist they just do. yes many of them have the nasty habit of manifesting literally. but that's the nature of magic in the cwod. people believe it therefore it exists. that's what the umbra is, that's what the dreaming is, that's what magic is. all a reflection of differing beliefs across vast spectrum of reality.each group has a &quot;secret truth&quot; that is actually a piece of a truth far more simple than any one's ego or cultural pride wants to admit. that everyone else's beliefs are just as valid as theirs.<br /> <br /> it just seems your trying to force a hundred square pegs into the same round hole at the same time. belief was never &quot;logical&quot; and it never had to be. the problems with crossovers was never really cosmological, it was pretty much mechanical. the fluff already had a built in coping mechanism to deal with the various inconsistencies. the crunch was the hard part.<br /> <br /> and i'm not pulling this out of my but either. this is a strong recuring theme in Mage, Changeling, and to a lesser extent Werewolf. Magic and even the vast cosmological effects were influenced by billions of people thinking of things throw in the extra supernatural nature of the critters all believing some thing and voila! Magic stew!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T08:13:05-07:00","id":146751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=146385#post146385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">too be honest there was never a problem with me in the inconsistencies between cosmologies. every critter in the cWOD is just like any other religion or belief system in the real world. they don't have to be compatible to co exist they just do. yes many of them have the nasty habit of manifesting literally. but that's the nature of magic in the cwod. people believe it therefore it exists. that's what the umbra is, that's what the dreaming is, that's what magic is. all a reflection of differing beliefs across vast spectrum of reality.each group has a &quot;secret truth&quot; that is actually a piece of a truth far more simple than any one's ego or cultural pride wants to admit. that everyone else's beliefs are just as valid as theirs.<br /> <br /> it just seems your trying to force a hundred square pegs into the same round hole at the same time. belief was never &quot;logical&quot; and it never had to be. the problems with crossovers was never really cosmological, it was pretty much mechanical. the fluff already had a built in coping mechanism to deal with the various inconsistencies. the crunch was the hard part.<br /> <br /> and i'm not pulling this out of my but either. this is a strong recuring theme in Mage, Changeling, and to a lesser extent Werewolf. Magic and even the vast cosmological effects were influenced by billions of people thinking of things throw in the extra supernatural nature of the critters all believing some thing and voila! Magic stew!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like that you broke it down into fluff vs crunch.<br /> <br /> I think like you and most others here do on the fluff... everything fits just fine, as different aspects of the same truth.<br /> <br /> On crunch I never had much of a problem either. I think perhaps because I was never interested in &quot;balance&quot; across the game lines (the disparity is what gave it an edge, crunch wise) and because Mage: the Ascension was easily my touchstone no matter what the PCs were. That combined with the fact that in table-top games as long as everyone is there for the same purpose (awesome stories, fun characters) we could always quickly find a resolution that was both fluff-accurate and reasonably fair.<br /> <br /> So with that being said, out of curiosity what sort of mechanical problems did you run into in your experience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T08:53:09-08:00","id":1432794,"title":"","content":"I think that it is probably simpler to use the Translation guides for Chronicles. Or try looking at this old project: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wod-3-0-a-collaborative-fan-project.568684/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...roject.568684/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","user":"ryu238","date":". 01-20-2021, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T11:51:21-08:00","id":1432813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/95460-a-more-logical-world-of-darkness?p=98503#post98503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you got some page references on this, actually? Because my 1st Ed. books were pretty saturated with crossovers too. Hell, that's when Samuel Haight was the focal point of the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've noticed that no one is addressing this. I'm aware Haight is/was very unpopular but still...<br /> <br /> A good way to create consistency would be to severely reduce the scale of metaplot events. Taking a cue from Chronicles, there would be no Gehenna, no Wyrm/Weaver based Apocalypse,...I just realized I am taking too much from Chronicles now \ud83d\ude33 \ud83d\ude05 <br /> <br /> Still Vampire 5th edition was forced to drop or hand-wave away Gehenna...perhaps something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","user":"ryu238","date":". 01-20-2021, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}